  "created": "2026-09-07T18:33:09.52Z",
  "description": "A CLI tool for managing GitHub Projects and Copilot-assigned issues in bulk. Define your project in a YAML file and let orcai create issues, assign them to Copilot, and clean up when done.",
  "id": "OrcAI.Tool",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-09-07T18:36:12.37Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "F2pcvpj4K7xc5afkni/OqdKTxJlZ7NjdptC6jwPa4cajSEvivBk5Caww1Q9X4+J+Pj+0c78j6eu4tlakLxWLQA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 3361944,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/dburriss/orca",
  "published": "2026-09-07T18:33:09.52Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "`orcai nudge`'s live GitHub fallback check (`FindPrsForIssue`) always returned no PRs found, for every issue, because its GraphQL query referenced `closingPullRequests`, a field that does not exist on GitHub's `Issue` type. The request errored and the error was silently swallowed into `[]`. Nudge could therefore reassign `@copilot` on issues that were already closed by a merged, correctly-linked PR, causing Copilot's cloud agent to open a duplicate PR for already-completed work. Fixed by querying the real field, `closedByPullRequestsReferences` (with `includeClosedPrs:true` to also surface merged/closed PRs).\n`orcai nudge` no longer falls back to assign-copilot behavior (unassign + reassign `@copilot`) for jobs whose `action.type` has no assignee concept, most notably `cmd-to-github` (where orcai itself opens the PR). Previously it silently defaulted to `@copilot` and reassigned it on already-closed issues; it now reports that these jobs must be re-triggered via `orcai run` instead.",
  "repository": {
